`give back`. This is real spec drift: `SPEC.md`'s return-value examples show `give back` inside `if`/`else`, and `tests/test_closures.rb:14` explicitly comments that `give back` does not leave a function in this build; `tests/test_functions.rb:53-62,140-145` only assert `type_of` or put the `give back` last, so no test pins early-return. This is pre-existing (the phase's `phases/phase-073/FINDINGS.md` reproduces it) and out of the test-only phase's scope, but it is still a live language bug that the phase ships and the review records. Traced, not run here; the FINDINGS.md reproduction is consistent with lines 2253 and 1095.  3. [MINOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:48 — `Expected::Number(want), Value::Number(got) => want == got` uses exact `f64` equality for the reference check. The values happen to be integer-valued, but a workload whose expected/actual diverge by one ULP (e.g. a different evaluation order between engines) is reported as `WrongAnswer` rather than a numeric mismatch. Use an integer/bit-exact representation or a documented tolerance for `Expected::Number`.  4. [MINOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:324 — `render_markdown` writes `row.answer` raw into a Markdown table cell. A text workload returning `|` or a newline would break the table, and `bench_md_exists_and_names_all_workloads` (tests/bench_test.rs:52-63) parses cells with a naive `split('|')`, so such a workload would fail the gate with a misleading message. Escape `|`/newlines when rendering the cell.  5. [MINOR] tests/bench/mod.rs:200-216 — a timeout returns `BudgetExceeded` but leaves the worker thread detached and uncancellable; `edge_a_hung_workload_fails_loudly_at_its_budget` (tests/bench_test.rs:226-239) therefore passes while a 250 ms sleeper keeps running after the test returns. Documented in the REPORT's known gaps and not fixable without a cancellation hook or child process, but the `resource_limit` row overstates the guarantee; the leap to a child process is the concrete fix.  REVIEW VERDICT: FINDINGS 5
